# sites-642.draft.kzs -- DRAFT logical sites of case C5 (nasa/cFE #72) for the instrumented family (kzs-sites 2,
# kairos/docs/event_semantics.md section 3) on the fixed release cFE 6.4.2 with OSAL 4.1.1 (posix) and the pc-linux
# PSP 1.2.0.0, built as the release readme says (research/cfs_procrace/plan/c5_execution_basis_20261028.md section 2).
# DRAFT: not used by any run.  Checked only by a single-unit compile with kzgcc 0.2 (that plan, section 6.3).  There is
# no F0 counterpart yet (the plan's section 7), so no equiv line.
#
# Same labels and site ids as sites-641.draft.kzs so the two versions compare label by label.  Sites 3 and 6 (the
# unlock before OS_TaskCreate and the re-lock after it) have no statement in 6.4.2: the fix removed them (6.4.1 ->
# 6.4.2 diff, cases/C5.md F9), so the ids are left out on purpose.  Paths are relative to cFE-6.4.2-OSS-release/
# (sha256 c64ed2aa...) with osal-4.1.1-release moved to osal/ (sha256 8f0f2b23...).  OSAL, cfe_sb_api.c and sample_app.c
# are byte-identical to the 6.4.1 tree, and EVS_GetAppID (cfe_evs_utils.c L122-L140) has the same lines (the file differs
# only from L615, the C3 guard); so those sites repeat the 6.4.1 lines.
# Nothing here is a research condition.
kzs-sites 2
source cfe rev=cFE-6.4.2-OSS-release ref="SourceForge coreflightexec cFE-6.4.2-OSS-release.tar.gz sha256 c64ed2aac910e79a641f49279dfdff3b7b49374e54ed56b595d47e16a3f53a4f"
source osal rev=osal-4.1.1-release ref="SourceForge osal osal-4.1.1-release.tar.gz sha256 8f0f2b23d8226256fdb8543bf9fcb560b38434411dc12cb4f7f35b9c19e61d46"
module 1 name=core-linux.bin source=cfe
module 2 name=sample_app.so source=cfe

